      "math_academy_id": "e-4718",
      "problem": "Find the inverse of the elementary matrix \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14228499/assets/47f842a2db349f380762c94e733a18cf5813d34e0f6b1f96f647601819abceb6.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "We write down $E$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{2}{5} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14228499/assets/47a29c46cf4f72aaff9bed86a960ed30fd045dec1eede3891c2a475e1d849b63.svg)",
